      "problem": "Let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}+1$ defined on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $G(x)=-9x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}+1∼1-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{18(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}}\nand\n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-9x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$",
